---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CallToAction from '../components/CallToAction.astro';
import { site } from '../site.config';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Nicolás Moreale is an AWS engineer in Buenos Aires working on data engineering, Amazon Connect contact centers and cloud infrastructure."
>
  <header class="wrap page-head">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>
      I'm Nicolás, an AWS engineer in Buenos Aires. I build data pipelines and data lakes, Amazon
      Connect contact centers, and the AWS infrastructure they run on.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="wrap columns">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        My focus is data engineering on AWS: pipelines that bring data in from databases, files and APIs,
        Glue and PySpark jobs that clean, validate and deduplicate it, and data lakes that business teams
        can query and report on with Athena and QuickSight. I was a data engineer at Cognizant, working on
        data pipelines, reporting and cloud operations, and I've also worked with Azure Data Factory,
        Synapse and Azure DevOps. I have a Bachelor's degree in Data Science from the University of the
        City of Buenos Aires.
      </p>
      <p>
        Since late 2025 I've also worked on Amazon Connect for pharmaceutical patient-support programs:
        contact flows and routing, SMS and voicemail, Salesforce Service Cloud Voice, Lambda and DynamoDB
        integrations, and the reporting on top. It's regulated work. A call that lands in the wrong queue
        or a service level that's calculated the wrong way is a real problem, so I test with real calls
        and write everything down. Before all this I built process automation at IBM.
      </p>
      <p>
        That mix is the point. Contact centers produce a lot of data and most teams use very little of
        it, and both the data and the contact center need an AWS account that is secure, automated and
        affordable. I work across all three. This website is a small example: it runs on my own AWS
        account, defined in AWS CDK, with no stored keys, for about a dollar a month.
        <a href="/work/this-website-on-aws/">How it's built</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        I work in English and Spanish, and also speak French, Italian and German. Buenos Aires keeps me on
        US hours, with a few hours of overlap with Europe every morning.
      </p>

      <h2>How I work</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Small, fixed-scope engagements with a written scope and price up front.</li>
        <li>Access through an IAM role you create and can revoke. No shared passwords.</li>
        <li>Changes tested before they reach production, and documented after.</li>
        <li>No client names in my case studies without permission.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <aside class="facts ui" aria-label="Background">
      <section>
        <h2>Experience</h2>
        <dl>
          <div>
            <dt>Syneos Health</dt>
            <dd>AWS and Amazon Connect engineer, 2025 to now</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Cognizant</dt>
            <dd>Data engineer, 2024 to 2025</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>IBM</dt>
            <dd>Automation developer, 2021 to 2022</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Education and credentials</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Bachelor's degree in Data Science, University of the City of Buenos Aires</li>
          <li>Information Systems Engineering, Universidad Tecnológica Nacional</li>
          <li>Machine Learning Specialization, DeepLearning.AI and Stanford Online</li>
          <li>Google Cloud: Building Batch Data Pipelines; Modernizing Data Lakes and Data Warehouses</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Elsewhere</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><a href={site.linkedin}>LinkedIn</a></li>
          {site.github && <li><a href={site.github}>GitHub</a></li>}
          <li><a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a></li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </aside>
  </div>

  <CallToAction />
</Base>

<style>
  .columns {
    display: grid;
    gap: 3rem 4rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 60rem) {
    .columns {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.6fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
      align-items: start;
    }
  }

  .facts {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2rem;
    font-size: 0.98rem;
  }

  .facts h2 {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    font-stretch: 92%;
    padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .facts dl {
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }

  .facts dt {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .facts dd {
    margin: 0.1rem 0 0;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .facts ul {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.6rem;
  }
</style>
